---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · Publisle"
  description="Learn how Publisle handles browser drafts, website visits, and information you send to the hosted MCP and PDF services."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="publisle-document mx-auto w-[70ch] space-y-8 py-10">
    <header class="space-y-3">
      <h1 class="font-display font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Effective <time datetime="2026-11-21">November 21, 2026</time>
      </p>
      <p>
        The Publisle maintainers operate publisle.xyz and its hosted MCP and PDF services.
        This policy explains what information those services use and how to contact us.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="browser-data" class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="browser-data" class="font-display font-semibold">Data in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        The playground runs editing and preview in your browser and uses local storage to
        save your draft on that device. The site also saves your theme preference in local
        storage. To remove these, clear the site data for publisle.xyz in your browser settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="hosted-services" class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="hosted-services" class="font-display font-semibold">Hosted MCP and PDF</h2>
      <p>
        The hosted API at api.publisle.xyz runs on OVHcloud. When you use hosted MCP, the
        API receives the tool arguments, including any document or text your client sends.
        The API processes each MCP request independently. The demo can also run MCP tools
        in your browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hosted PDF export sends your document content, metadata such as author names,
        and export options to the API so it can return a PDF. The service may request
        public images referenced in the document from the servers that host them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="retention" class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="retention" class="font-display font-semibold">Request logs and retention</h2>
      <p>
        The API uses IP addresses to enforce request and compilation limits. The
        application logs request timings and outcomes to help troubleshoot the service.
        Hosting and proxy logs may include IP addresses and basic request information,
        such as the time, path, and response status. Log retention depends on the hosting
        and logging settings and on operational needs.
      </p>
      <p>
        PDF jobs use temporary working files that the service cleans up when the job ends.
        When PDF caching is enabled, the service keeps generated PDFs and diagnostics so
        it can answer identical requests faster. By default, a cached result can be reused
        for up to one hour. Cached files can remain on disk until storage eviction or
        maintenance removes them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="third-parties" class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="third-parties" class="font-display font-semibold">Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub Pages hosts the website and logs visitor IP addresses for security.
        Your browser also contacts GitHub to display the repository’s star count.
        See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where a page displays a YouTube or Vimeo embed, the player can contact that
        provider. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en">Google’s privacy policy</a>
        for YouTube and <a href="https://vimeo.com/legal/privacy/policy">Vimeo’s privacy policy</a>.
        If you connect an assistant or another MCP client, its own privacy practices
        apply to the information it handles.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact" class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="privacy-contact" class="font-display font-semibold">Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on the law that applies to you, you may have the right to access,
        correct, or delete personal information, restrict or object to its use, or
        complain to a data protection authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or requests, email the maintainers at{" "}
        <a href="mailto:privacy@voidreg.xyz">privacy@voidreg.xyz</a>. We use the
        information you send to respond and handle your request.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
